The rule says a capability declares "for all seven hosts (`cli`, `macos`, …) a state in `lib/src/hosts/host_capability_profile.dart`". The *record types and validation* live there, but the seven built-in profiles — where those states are actually declared and where a contributor would go to add a new cell — are constructed in `lib/src/hosts/host_wiring_builder.dart` (`cliProfile` … `builtInProfiles`). Future contributors (and agents) following this instruction will open the wrong file first. Suggest: "…a state in `lib/src/hosts/` — the built-in profiles in `host_wiring_builder.dart`, validated by `host_capability_profile.dart`".
